  "2026-11-27T10:45:22.778Z",codex-agent,"Reproduce pending-only drift before edits. Trace the SDK, standalone and host check paths, preserve exact versioned comparison, and verify the package release scripts with a pending package version."
  "2026-11-27T10:46:18.186Z",codex-agent,"Reproduced on 6617b03: two dated tags, committed versioned changelog, then a single chore(deps) bump. File check exited 1 (tracker_changed); the entire diff added only Unreleased / Dependencies / Bump pending package from 2 to 3. Baseline repository changelog:check passed."
  "2026-11-27T10:54:40.368Z",codex-agent,"Implemented the comparison in the SDK file check, using the generator's Markdown section boundaries. Both command entry points report pending_only and honor --check-pending. Two branches, both Dependabot squash-subject cases, strict mode, versioned corruption, and non-Git SDK/host parity passed in the fixed fixtures."
  "2026-11-27T11:01:00.014Z",codex-agent,"Verified four external scripts perform their own whole-file comparisons. Follow-up unbraind/pm-changelog#385 tracks pm-ops, pm-slack, pm-gantt-chart and pm-review with immutable source links. The direct package check remains the only implementation changed here."
  "2026-11-27T11:06:22.370Z",codex-agent,"Release rehearsal in a disposable full clone: changed package.json from 2026.11.24 to 2026.11.27 and added a synthetic dependency commit. The repository changelog:full wrote '## 2026.11.27 - 2026-11-27' with the 1 to 2 range and PR link. changelog:check passed without writing. Editing the release entry to 1 to 3 failed (exit 1, tracker_changed); regeneration restored SHA-256 8ddf1cef075b69e4c6ac8354d83d835520c714de7ff938e93b38e16648b26528."
  "2026-11-27T11:06:30.306Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral reverts in a disposable package: restoring whole-file comparison failed 5 acceptance cases (including both #382 squash cases and concurrent integration); accepting versioned edits failed 3; dropping strict comparison failed 2; omitting the standalone receipt, host advisory or release note each failed 1. Baseline files and tests were retained. Source and test typechecks and docstring lint passed. The optional fleet ESLint comparison found 9 pre-existing diagnostics on both base and head and no new diagnostic."
  "2026-11-27T11:10:09.127Z",codex-agent,"All restored controls passed (6/6). Additional exact-build reverts: disabling pending comparison failed all 3 selected property/SDK/installed-host checks; dropping the final pending separator rule failed the non-Git case. Restored 3/3. The registered pm test command passed 8/8 with zero skips, including decoded host JSON and TOON and 32 deterministic mixed pending/released edits."
  "2026-11-27T11:10:14.920Z",codex-agent,"Actual npm and Bun installs from one tarball each passed 7/7 verdicts across the SDK, standalone and pm host, with both host receipt formats decoded and file bytes retained. Verified all 115 tar members and installed contents; SHA-256 8c30bae78d1681bbd83ca95f1a75239e332a4955eed550328544f85baa9f975f. Package content scan: 115 files, zero findings."
  "2026-11-27T11:17:45.813Z",codex-agent,Repeated the pending-version release rehearsal after syncing main and rebuilding the final package. Full/check passed and the mutated release range failed. The restored complete file on this base has SHA-256 9c6a2bdfd1da289cc40f80d38971bbe6763fca0e58128ad29571f9362147e7ce. A separate local pm health read reports the same globally available pm-github host version skew and legacy 32 provenance records in a base clone.
  "2026-11-27T11:30:30.931Z",codex-agent,"Targeted local gate passed 1052/1052 tests in 39 suites across 56 test files with zero skips or cancellations. Ran node --test --test-concurrency=2 on touched files and references at the repository's quick CI depth. The dedicated in-process human-output assertion also passed after its addition. Source/test compilation, typecheck, docstring lint, release rehearsal and installed artifact checks passed. Coverage and complete npm/Bun release gates remain for CI at their existing thresholds."
  "2026-11-27T12:06:09.303Z",codex-agent,"Reopened work for CodeRabbit review 6087820042. Main is already integrated. Checking whether Markdown-escaped bracket labels bypass the shared release heading identity and covering the same identity in read-only checks, prepend cleanup, promotion, replacement, and structured receipts."
  "2026-11-27T12:11:33.053Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed the review finding on the previous head with a non-Git tracker and the installed pm host. The governing rule is that all stored Markdown release headings share one label parser for semantic identity. The parser now accepts escaped outer brackets, preserves malformed and literal link-like text, and feeds comparison, prepend cleanup, promotion, replacement, sorting, standalone summaries, structured projections, contract reports, and tagged dependency lookup. The strict check still compares the complete Markdown."
  "2026-11-27T12:12:31.749Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof for review 6087820042, in a disposable copy. The four selected tests passed. Restoring only the bracket parser and rebuilding dist made all four fail with assertions, including the installed JSON/TOON host. Restoring only the raw tagged publication lookup failed its projection regression. Restoring only the raw summary formatter failed the summary regression. After restoring and rebuilding, all four passed again. The corpus covers plain and singly/doubly escaped delimiters, optional dates, malformed labels, escaped link-like suffixes, and strict checks."
  "2026-11-27T12:14:10.628Z",codex-agent,"The round-one package archive matched all 115 files in the checkout, archive, and both consumer installs. Node with npm and Bun each passed nine checks on a fresh non-Git tracker, covering SDK read/strict/write-merge behavior, summary labels, standalone JSON, and installed host JSON/TOON with read-only strict failure. Archive SHA-256 bdeda34613322cf4f39be3f9745d748967243674bb1bd66e1c90d9fb3fa4bf50. The package privacy scan reported zero failures."
  "2026-11-27T12:28:53.142Z",codex-agent,"Scope correction after the broader suite. The tagged dependency lookup is a separate publication rule. The existing near-match regression requires a canonical heading at the tag, so a semantic label match must never authorize publication. Restored that original comparison and proof script. The added real Git test covers the canonical heading and all four bracket spellings across Markdown, document, and summary generation. The normalized parser remains shared for semantic comparison and summary display."
  "2026-11-27T12:40:43.416Z",codex-agent,"Final scoped revert proof supersedes the exploratory tagged lookup change. Eight focused tests passed, including all four existing near-match tests. In a disposable copy, the old bracket parser with rebuilt dist failed three regressions, the raw summary fallback failed one, and broadening the canonical publication witness failed the new guard. The four fixed controls passed before and after the mutations. The original publication witness remains in the patch base."
  "2026-11-27T12:55:26.059Z",codex-agent,"Final review gates passed. Targeted Node tests with two workers passed 756/756 across 25 files, without skips. The pinned pm test runner passed both linked commands (11/11 and 2/2). Typecheck, source/test builds and docstring lint (306 declarations) passed. Fleet ESLint reported six existing diagnostics on the two touched TypeScript files and no new ones. The final archive SHA-256 is d3a3d0ad558829fde3e92963bac7197205411cff3c9899c77e68bddbfb6178c9, superseding the exploratory archive. All 115 packed files matched both installations. npm and Bun each passed nine consumer checks and package privacy scanning found zero failures. CodeRabbit re-review will be requested on the pushed head."
  "2026-11-27T13:24:12.633Z",codex-agent,"Review thread PRRT_kwDOSfkApc68zDlg. Main is already included and the follow-up item is open and unclaimed. The comparison must use the section boundaries and end-of-file whitespace rules of the writer that produced its candidate. Checking both merge modes, historical profiles, and the shared standalone and pm-host paths."
  "2026-11-27T13:27:46.210Z",codex-agent,"Reproduced the wrong verdict in both directions on the previous head. With a fenced versioned heading under pending text, an older writer changed a release and the modern comparison returned pending_only. A terminal hard break also made a pending-only historical prepend fail. Both modes now scan headings with the selected profile and prepend uses its terminal trim. The SDK, standalone and pm host file checks share this comparator. Historical CLI diagnostics compare full writer output, and the exact canonical tagged publication witness is a separate policy. The two tests cover all five profiles, both fence types, four bracket spellings, read-only strict checks and legacy/current whitespace. In a disposable copy, restoring the default scanner failed only the heading test, and restoring the default trim failed only the whitespace test. Both passed before and after the mutations."
  "2026-11-27T13:45:42.039Z",codex-agent,"Local round-two gates passed with at most two test workers. The affected test set passed 758/758 across 25 files with zero skips. The pinned tracker runner passed its three linked commands (13/13, 2/2, 2/2). Typecheck, source and test builds, docstring lint (306 declarations), and the 115-file package content scan passed. Fleet ESLint found six baseline diagnostics across the two changed TypeScript files and zero new ones. The packed archive SHA-256 65041dc302cd8d6b4770640ae5e5742f61f07ffac707caa49fb5804841e67b1c matched all 115 installed files in npm and Bun, with 11/11 checks per runtime on non-Git trackers covering historical SDK checks and current standalone and host JSON/TOON."
